WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:14.466
Hi! In visual text comprehension, you get a poster, an advert or a notice, and then some multiple-choice questions. The answers are all in the picture. You just need to know where to look.

2
00:00:14.616 --> 00:00:20.034
First read the title to find out what it is about: a fun fair at Green Park.

3
00:00:20.184 --> 00:00:29.394
Next read the big words: the date is Saturday, 6 December, the time is 10 a.m. to 4 p.m., and tickets cost two dollars.

4
00:00:29.544 --> 00:00:38.082
Then read the small print, especially anything with a star. Children under five enter free. Many questions test this.

5
00:00:38.232 --> 00:00:45.378
Finally, think about why it was made. It is to invite people to come to the fun fair.

6
00:00:45.528 --> 00:00:51.258
Read the question first, circle the key words, then look back at the visual text.

7
00:00:51.408 --> 00:00:56.394
For questions about money or time, write the numbers down and work it out.

8
00:00:56.544 --> 00:01:02.946
Look at all four options, and use the information to cross out the wrong ones.

9
00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:08.778
Watch out! Many pupils read only the big words and miss the small print!

10
00:01:08.928 --> 00:01:16.218
The star says children under five enter free. You need this when a question asks about a young child's ticket.

11
00:01:16.368 --> 00:01:20.922
So read every word in the visual text.

12
00:01:21.072 --> 00:01:29.370
Your turn! What time does the magic show start? Pause and think.

13
00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:34.242
At 2 p.m. Did you get it right?

14
00:01:34.392 --> 00:01:42.522
Here's another! On which day is the fun fair? Pause and think.

15
00:01:42.672 --> 00:01:50.370
On Saturday, 6 December. It is written just below the title. Did you get it right?

16
00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:58.698
One more! How many hours is the fair open? Pause and think.

17
00:01:58.848 --> 00:02:10.458
Six hours. From 10 a.m. to noon is two hours, and from noon to 4 p.m. is four hours. Two plus four is six. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:10.608 --> 00:02:18.930
Another one! How much does a four-year-old pay? Pause and think.

19
00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:27.426
Nothing. Four is under five, and the star says children under five enter free. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:27.576 --> 00:02:38.754
Next one! Two adults and a child aged eight go to the fair. How much do they pay altogether? Pause and think.

21
00:02:38.904 --> 00:02:49.770
Six dollars. Eight is not under five, so all three need tickets. Three times two dollars is six dollars. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:57.786
Last one! Why was this poster made? Pause and think.

23
00:02:57.936 --> 00:03:06.762
To invite people to the fun fair. The last line, come and join the fun, tells us too. Did you get it right?

24
00:03:06.912 --> 00:03:14.802
Remember: read the title, then the big words and the small print, and don't miss the star. Then think about its purpose.

25
00:03:14.952 --> 00:03:19.698
Write down numbers for money and time, and check all four options.

26
00:03:19.848 --> 00:03:26.106
Next time you see a poster, test yourself by finding the time and place!

